From 54855e65aa33d6cba73cf066ea5d9ea37dc9401f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:08:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: Do not lose DSP requests across system suspend

A userspace FastRPC invoke waits with wait_for_completion_interruptible().
When the system suspends, the freezer interrupts that wait; the invoke
returns -ERESTARTSYS, its context stays queued on the DSP, and the ioctl is
restarted, which sends a second invoke. The DSP later completes the first,
orphaned context, and its reply is dropped.

For a reverse-RPC listener (adsprpcd, the audio PD) the reply of its
"next" invoke is the DSP's next request, so one DSP request is lost per
suspend. On the Xiaomi 12T Pro (SM8475) the ADSP's voice graph loads its
Fluence modules through the audio PD; after N suspends the next N graph
opens fail (the DSP waits for a file read that never arrives), so calls
have no audio until enough failed attempts have drained the orphans.

Wait in TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE | TASK_FREEZABLE instead: the freezer then
freezes the task in place, real signals still interrupt the wait.

Device-tested on the Xiaomi 12T Pro.

Signed-off-by: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/misc/fastrpc.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
index d7a9e12f5..832c9b7b8 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -1278,7 +1278,15 @@ static int fastrpc_internal_invoke(struct fastrpc_user *fl,  u32 kernel,
 		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&ctx->work, 10 * HZ))
 			err = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	} else {
-		err = wait_for_completion_interruptible(&ctx->work);
+		/*
+		 * Freezable: the freezer must not interrupt the wait. On
+		 * -ERESTARTSYS the context stays queued on the DSP and the
+		 * restarted ioctl sends a second one; the DSP then completes the
+		 * orphaned context and its reply (for a listener thread: the
+		 * DSP's next reverse-RPC request) is lost, once per suspend.
+		 */
+		err = wait_for_completion_state(&ctx->work,
+						TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE | TASK_FREEZABLE);
 	}
 
 	if (err)
-- 
2.55.0

